  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Buna--<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math> stand for styrene.</p><p>Buna &ndash; S is a more commonly used name for a polymer named styrene butadiene rubber. The structure of Buna &ndash; S is given by:</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0041_281661eff8fd.png\" style=\"width: 664px; height: 143px;\" /></p><p>Buna &ndash; S is formed using the monomers butadiene and styrene.</p><p>Thus in&nbsp;Buna &ndash; S, the Bu stands for Butadiene, since butadiene is one of the constituent monomers of the given polymer. Also, Na stands for sodium and S represents the monomer Styrene used for the synthesis of the given polymer.</p>"
